"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ACV7M","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T21:45:44Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T21:45:44Z","body":"cc @TokageItLab ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3221839564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237264009","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109968#issuecomment-3237264009","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109968","id":3237264009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A9LqJ","user":{"login":"oakstendheim","id":212953646,"node_id":"U_kgDODLFqLg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/212953646?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim","html_url":"https://github.com/oakstendheim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oakstendheim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T14:39:10Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:39:10Z","body":"I found that you can fix this issue by using a custom timeline for the animations in the blendspace:\n\n<img width=\"455\" height=\"475\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b720c0b0-988b-434e-ae41-45335bf91daa\" />\n\nBefore:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/592b303e-8d43-4a63-bbf7-e5f9646aa77f\n\nAfter:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7723e9b5-e3ab-47f2-809e-91770f6e54f3","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237264009/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237586757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109968#issuecomment-3237586757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109968","id":3237586757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A-adF","user":{"login":"Xiexe","id":5119787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTk3ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5119787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe","html_url":"https://github.com/Xiexe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T16:25:00Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T16:25:00Z","body":"> I found that you can fix this issue by using a custom timeline for the animations in the blendspace:\n> \n> <img width=\"455\" height=\"475\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b720c0b0-988b-434e-ae41-45335bf91daa\" />\n> \n> Before:\n> \n> https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/592b303e-8d43-4a63-bbf7-e5f9646aa77f\n> \n> After:\n> \n> https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7723e9b5-e3ab-47f2-809e-91770f6e54f3\n\nThis isn't really a valid solution as it slows down the intended gate of the jog cycle to match the gate of the run cycle.\n\nUnity does do this, but it handles the mismatch internally, and dynamically, meaning that while you're fully in the walking state, the jogging state is slowed down, while if you're fully in the jogging state, the walking state is sped up. If you're somewhere in between, they're sped up/down proportional to the difference between them and where you are in the blend.\n\nThat ensures that the intended speed of the animation is maintained without having to manually handle it","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237586757/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272224933","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109968#issuecomment-3272224933","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109968","id":3272224933,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DCjCl","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-09T20:50:58Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T21:18:47Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/87171#issuecomment-2192099823\n\nHere I explained how it works. The current blocker for blending is that it cannot guarantee the exact animation length because it might nest BlendSpaces, BlendTree and StateMachine or similar components.\n\nSince other engines' Blend should not permit nesting, then automatically calculating this can guarantee synchronization (Or it may simply be allowing cases where synchronization breaks). However, Godot allows nesting, so it cannot guarantee that synchronization will not break, and automating this is not possible safely.\n\nIf we want to automate this, we'd likely need a restriction: BlendSpace should not nest other BlendSpaces, BlendTree and StateMachine - In other words, if those are nested, an error would be output and Blend should be aborted or it will notify a warning and break synchronization. The same applies when they are connected to Blend2/Blend3.\n\nMaking that an option might be possible (such as by making Sync an enum like `None,Loose,Hard`), but as I commented on a similar point in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11682, adding a separate AnimationNode is also one viable approach like https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/34179. And it should be opened as a proposal rather than an issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272224933/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]